15:24.784 --> 15:28.484
Wow, look at you. All that power
and you've still got that body.

15:28.591 --> 15:31.790
And the first thing I'm gonna do as mayor
is clean up Lake Quahog.

15:31.896 --> 15:33.831
Well, I know the people
will support you, Lois,

15:33.932 --> 15:37.132
because you connect with them,
like Disney connects with its audience.

15:37.305 --> 15:40.207
<i>- You the cow!
- No, you the cow!</i>

15:40.309 --> 15:42.006
Wow, Disney gets us!

15:45.050 --> 15:46.280
And I think we all realize

15:46.387 --> 15:48.652
the importance of stopping
the environmental damage

15:48.757 --> 15:50.192
being done to Lake Quahog.

15:50.294 --> 15:53.594
Which is why I'm proposing
a very modest tax increase

15:53.698 --> 15:54.723
that will help us to...

15:54.834 --> 15:55.802
(ALL BOOING)

15:55.903 --> 15:58.897
No, no, no. That's awful.
No, no, no. I'm not okay with that.

15:59.008 --> 16:02.104
- No new taxes.
- ALL: No new taxes!

16:02.213 --> 16:05.309
No new taxes! No new taxes!

16:05.451 --> 16:07.944
But what about the terrorists?

16:08.056 --> 16:09.115
(ALL GASP)

16:09.225 --> 16:11.991
That's right. Terrorists.

16:12.096 --> 16:15.534
We have intelligence that suggests

16:15.635 --> 16:18.435
that Hitler is plotting with...

16:19.308 --> 16:23.681
With the Legion of Doom
to assassinate Jesus.

16:25.017 --> 16:26.508
Using the lake as a base.

16:26.621 --> 16:28.521
(ALL MURMURING)

16:28.724 --> 16:31.194
<i>ANNOUNCER: Meanwhile,
at the Legion of Doom...</i>

16:32.096 --> 16:34.191
How did she discover our plan?

16:34.300 --> 16:37.931
Me, Solomon Grundy,
kind of dropped the ball on that one.

16:38.340 --> 16:40.071
And we also have evidence

16:40.177 --> 16:45.345
that Darth Vader tried
to buy yellowcake uranium

16:45.452 --> 16:48.048
from unwed teenage mothers.

16:48.156 --> 16:49.886
Those things all sound scary!

16:49.994 --> 16:52.293
How much money
before I can feel safe again?

16:52.397 --> 16:53.888
(STAMMERS)

16:54.133 --> 16:55.829
A hundred thousand?

16:55.936 --> 16:57.963
(ALL MURMURING)

16:58.140 --> 17:01.134
I threw a 10!
See that 10 there? I threw that.

17:06.120 --> 17:08.784
<i>At the top of the news,
Lake Quahog is once again clean</i>

17:08.924 --> 17:11.918
<i>thanks to the efforts
of newly-elected Mayor Lois Griffin.</i>

17:12.030 --> 17:14.432
<i>We now go to Asian reporter
Tricia Takanawa</i>

17:14.534 --> 17:16.025
<i>for her slant on the story.</i>

17:16.137 --> 17:17.162
<i>Thanks, Tom.</i>

17:17.272 --> 17:21.335
<i>Once again, happy locals are frolicking
in the waters of Lake Quahog,</i>

17:21.445 --> 17:23.575
<i>and we're here with their reactions.</i>

17:23.684 --> 17:26.175
<i>Sir, how does it feel to have the lake back?</i>

17:26.286 --> 17:28.313
<i>Well, I'll tell you, Tricia, as a local resident,</i>

17:28.424 --> 17:30.758
<i>I feel like I can once again take pride
in my community.</i>

17:30.861 --> 17:33.661
<i>I think this is really gonna
revitalize tourism, and...</i>

17:34.567 --> 17:37.164
<i>And, if you look around, I think
even the wildlife is starting to come back.</i>

17:37.273 --> 17:39.138
<i>And, you know, that's something
we haven't seen in a while</i>

17:39.241 --> 17:40.937
<i>and I think we're gonna be seeing
a lot more of that.</i>

17:41.345 --> 17:42.335
Hey, you guys.

17:42.448 --> 17:46.216
Mom, everyone on TV says
you're running the town great.

17:46.320 --> 17:48.585
Maybe you could do some damn laundry
once in a while.

17:48.690 --> 17:49.715
- What?
- What?

17:49.826 --> 17:53.890
- Wow, Mom, is that a new purse?
- Yeah, that looks pretty expensive.

17:53.999 --> 17:56.697
Well, don't tell anybody, Brian,
but I was a little naughty.

17:56.804 --> 17:57.794
(CHUCKLING)

17:57.906 --> 17:59.932
I may have dipped into the tax surplus.

18:00.043 --> 18:03.379
Wait a minute. You used taxpayer money
to buy yourself a handbag?

18:03.483 --> 18:05.281
It's no big deal, Brian.

18:05.385 --> 18:08.117
Besides, there was a lot left over
after the lake clean-up,

18:08.224 --> 18:11.662
and I figured
maybe I earned a little treat, huh?

18:11.763 --> 18:14.290
Lois, spending even one penny
of that money on yourself

18:14.400 --> 18:18.134
- is incredibly unethical.
- Oh, come on, it was only 600.

18:18.241 --> 18:21.838
My God, that's more than I spent
to go see that prize fight in Vegas.

18:22.013 --> 18:24.711
<i>I thought you said we was going
to see Hairspray.</i>

18:24.818 --> 18:27.755
Bitch, I thought I said just shut up
and be looking fine.

18:33.565 --> 18:35.432
What the hell's up
with these rolling blackouts?

18:35.536 --> 18:36.970
Well, since Lois is the mayor,

18:37.071 --> 18:39.234
I'm allowed to reroute
all the town's electricity.

18:39.342 --> 18:41.709
- What'd you do that for?
- So I could reanimate the corpse

18:41.813 --> 18:43.783
- of Jim Varney.
- Howdy, Vern.

18:43.883 --> 18:46.614
This is some dad-gum nice house
you got here, Vern.

18:46.720 --> 18:48.656
That's Vern-Vern-Vern-Vern.

18:48.791 --> 18:51.887
Oh, wait, wait. It was John Belushi.
That's who I wanted.

18:51.996 --> 18:53.658
- Peter, how could you...
- Way ahead of you, Brian.

18:53.766 --> 18:56.236
My mistake. I'll take care of this.

18:57.974 --> 19:01.776
- Hey, Jim, come out in the yard, will you?
- Sure thing, Vern.

19:05.085 --> 19:06.576
(GUN FIRING)

19:07.055 --> 19:08.114
He got the shotgun, Brian!

19:08.224 --> 19:10.524
Don't ask me how he did it,
but Jim Varney got the shotgun!

19:10.628 --> 19:11.596
- Run for your life!
- What?

19:11.697 --> 19:12.686
Run!

19:20.077 --> 19:23.310
- Excuse me, how much is this coat?
- It's 4,300.

19:23.415 --> 19:27.718
Oh. Do you think you can give me
a little mayoral discount?

19:27.823 --> 19:31.853
Well, I think you're doing a great job,
Mrs. Griffin, but my boss would kill me.

19:31.963 --> 19:34.125
- How's everything going out here?
- Fine, Mr. Voorhees.

19:34.233 --> 19:36.829
Good. 'Cause if you screw up, I'll kill you.

19:36.939 --> 19:39.033
Hi, Bob Grossbeard, Quahog Oil.

19:39.142 --> 19:42.136
- I'd like to buy you that coat.
- Really?

19:42.247 --> 19:45.218
All I ask in return
is that you let my company do

19:45.319 --> 19:47.288
just a little bit of dumping in your lake.

19:47.389 --> 19:50.121
This guy don't sit right with me, Lois.
He don't sit right with me.

19:50.227 --> 19:54.759
- But I just cleaned up Quahog lake.
- Do you want the coat or not?

19:59.343 --> 20:02.644
- I want the coat.
- Excellent. Then we have a deal.

20:02.915 --> 20:03.883
(SIGHS)

20:03.984 --> 20:06.886
Brian's gonna be really upset
when he finds out.

20:06.988 --> 20:09.425
I'll just take him for a ride in the car,
he'll forget all about it.

20:11.128 --> 20:12.426
(SNIFFING)

20:12.532 --> 20:15.161
Wait a minute, I know where we are.
The park is near here!

20:15.269 --> 20:17.934
We're near the park, Lois!
That's the tree, I peed on that!

20:18.041 --> 20:19.065
Hey, hey, Lois! Lois!

20:20.758 --> 20:22.022
There's another dog in that car!

20:22.128 --> 20:24.290
Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey!
There's another dog in that car!

20:24.398 --> 20:27.369
Hey! Are you seeing that?
Hey! Hey! Hey, other dog! Fuck you!

20:31.495 --> 20:34.864
Ladies and gentlemen,
on behalf of the Quahog Oil Refinery,

20:34.967 --> 20:39.201
we would like to thank Mayor Lois Griffin
for our newest waste pipe.

20:42.345 --> 20:43.939
(ALL CHEERING)

20:44.049 --> 20:45.381
Let the dumping resume!

20:52.497 --> 20:54.557
- What's going on?
- Everybody dead.

20:54.667 --> 20:57.035
Oh, see now.
You know who they gonna blame this on.

20:57.139 --> 20:58.767
Mmm-hmm. The black dolphins.

20:58.875 --> 21:01.869
See, the honky dolphin always trying
to keep the black dolphin down.

21:01.980 --> 21:03.949
I mean, can't we all just swim along?

21:04.050 --> 21:06.885
You know what I'm gonna do?
I'm gonna call Fishy Jackson.

21:06.988 --> 21:09.321
And you know what?
I'm gonna call Catfish Sharpton.

21:09.426 --> 21:10.450
Get them motherfuckers on the line.

21:12.540 --> 21:13.199
Hey, Jake,

21:13.308 --> 21:15.005
how long can you hold
your breath underwater?

21:15.111 --> 21:17.307
Longer than you! Check it out!

21:20.253 --> 21:22.085
(BOTH SCREAMING)

21:22.189 --> 21:23.384
My face!

21:23.525 --> 21:25.324
(SCREAMING)

21:30.470 --> 21:34.932
- Lois, what the hell are you doing?
- Remembering who I am, you crook!

21:35.044 --> 21:38.539
Oh, I'm a crook, am I?
What about all the money you embezzled?

21:38.651 --> 21:40.744
Do you want people to find out
about that?

21:40.853 --> 21:44.155
You better play ball
or we'll find someone else who will.

21:44.259 --> 21:45.693
I'll play ball.

21:45.795 --> 21:48.595
You know what, West?
You can have your job back.

21:48.700 --> 21:51.671
Politics does terrible things
to good people.

21:51.773 --> 21:54.367
Good for you, Lois.
You wised up before it was too late.

21:54.476 --> 21:56.913
I was so consumed by power and money,

21:57.015 --> 21:59.679
I became the very thing
I set out to destroy.

21:59.786 --> 22:02.517
Hooray, I'm mayor again!

22:02.623 --> 22:05.424
Don't we need to have
a whole new election?

22:07.197 --> 22:10.101
There. Now no one
will have heard him say that.

22:10.203 --> 22:12.138
We all heard him say it.

22:13.542 --> 22:17.241
- Anybody else hear anything?
- My wife did.

22:19.552 --> 22:20.644
(GUN FIRING)

22:20.645 --> 23:21.645
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru